[{"id":"VRCE-5-10-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":1,"english":"Remaining in that mansion, (Hanuman) desirous of getting a sight of Sītā graced with a fair presence, went into bowers, and picture galleries, and night-houses;* but her he did not find. *Intended for stay at night.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"612072f4574574dc0330c7cd0b67534748cbdea460a2b248f5a1b2bff8ff659f","compact":"ae728eaecf97881a45a002db2f87bc7f83fd103d22ec1d098f6b01aa7e4e3e77","nasal":"e0b12d3e4679225bd2916e49ad80d99b1d7eb2d88352ccac7da172287c9c9f1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":2,"english":"And not finding the beloved (spouse) of Raghu's son that mighty monkey reflected, “Surely Sītā is not alive, for although I have searched (through and through), yet Mithila's daughter I have failed to find.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ac08595134d4bdce7d6ec7bbb0671682770adc505161e21b60a20c7ad344bae","compact":"53c41c8f324ef3458b656e800be50f2fcf19b82b59864ae04a625260e0e606b6","nasal":"9e9e7bcf48ae40e92dac38979e83057eeef8088c2b200ad3d78bba7d46552fea"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":3,"english":"That girl solicitous for the preservation of her chastity, and staying in the prime path of virtuous woman, that chaste one has, for certain, been slain by this chief of the Rākṣasas, (ever) finding delight in iniquity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"76937fde21168c4a3af851777c96f5ee477aef2b03caa0623b206e3c121dc341","compact":"162091f0b1ef319563493bda4ac6eea5f5ba17fcc629f5a853d708d792d540e7","nasal":"162091f0b1ef319563493bda4ac6eea5f5ba17fcc629f5a853d708d792d540e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":4,"english":"Seeing the wives of the Rākṣasa inonarch, of frightful forms, monstrous; of lurid hue; having huge faces; with large horrid eyes, the daughter of Janaka has given up the ghost from fright.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.911,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee0f23bb73beceedcbfc68ba08fb69d021a065087b752f35766d5c48e797f526","compact":"e8db40b8cb91f5de2753f4bf3f60b2cd3db64e90abb51674f36a480d35978762","nasal":"e8db40b8cb91f5de2753f4bf3f60b2cd3db64e90abb51674f36a480d35978762"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":5,"english":"Failing to see Sītā, and (thereby) annulling my prowess, and having long spent the appointed space in company with the monkeys, way have I none to present myself before Sugrīva, that monkey being puissant and given to meting out sharp chastisement.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0525d08214931e601426a4c95484edf5d02801dad8650f45e23dbfc99bd9c90c","compact":"042b7e56a97e8753a21944c41027b9b56bbad138da6a4925645e227c39a7d78f","nasal":"0aaa0544118c20f65de4f9cac4397935e358bde2b32572c54b8eb43be8de2e6b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":6,"english":"Having searched the inner apartment through, and seen the wives of the Rākṣasa, I do not see the chaste Sită. Therefore vain is the trouble that I take.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11e307a7706f0218ec48088506058c1629224367d6a81ab8da04c40c8460a264","compact":"2d5e03f4b0dad71348103d49105edab4a2839a3260166bcc11d7420882c0e68f","nasal":"e8a2d5cec4487e63df50d7d09e085a6436090250d834aa391cd7c7ea9f027354"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":7,"english":"What, alas! shall the monkeys assembled tell me when I shall go (to them)? 'O hero, tell us what you have done, repairing there.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22d3fe5d2718422756feb826b8d7be831ad50bd456a94fe9ad3256ade3445619","compact":"3e01ee591d7875a93bdb21cb4406c047e0c3d6eb4e8c481196951cadd68de539","nasal":"ca79c7a83b0b1386d2751414dfea413f93c65b0f66a4984928382d0029cba99c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":8,"english":"And not having seen Janaka's daughter, what shall I answer? The term fixed (by Sugrīva) having been past, certainly meet it is that I should fast to death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.792,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fe12b14227b238b7e7199f8456da1afe950b069a32462169d277c4e058ca2a96","compact":"5eaca6e33ba00dd0eb6d7f0ad5d8daddbbe3404c1c6880d453aebb48a2929647","nasal":"bf14c3bddf9dff02bc301956a7aad0599ec8d33c025bb0efd0355da736128b9d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":9,"english":"And what shall the aged Jambhavan, and what shall Angada, say? And what, again, shall the assembled monkeys say to me when I shall have crossed over the main.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a958d7f7f24c979af70f583dc8d5b5f66ddba4ea9de7e708c494b3ed803b336c","compact":"9b33f41b83d9f1047e4c95c638c4258d640c02d18334a15d8a7f83485bd1450b","nasal":"ff518a2da9a78282a34b97c69d2ec44d40e4e179965689e23441a5f6d6868d6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":10,"english":"But perseverance is the source of good fortune; and perseverance bring about supreme happiness. Search again I will, where I have not yet searched.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.823,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a29293f50283fda41e13b9cb4e67381aba2bc0f088e8fbb8c3988ab65247ff50","compact":"c27aec28e9e50a1aef473340646ff5472bcd55e79c12531adb756f61185d7dcf","nasal":"ac957002ff39caa84d30b4930df98fbddd7485c3d95048f4a425cfd0d4c32db0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":11,"english":"Perseverance, for certain, ever bring people to all profitable objects. Whatever one dose with vigour, bear fruit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"35c719203aa262b697a700a9e36b613724c74072b125d853d6da8841f8d10ff1","compact":"dca6c54216871431e5dd7210ced4e954ed207c8544b9fd1d9dc347455c2f95a1","nasal":"a6c52571c259b58748eaad562e0670f8bcbe18139a7a3c0f880a1b3317e48bd1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":12,"english":"Therefore will I put forth fresh dear efforts vigorously. I will search such places held by Rāvana as I have not yet seen.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"94bdaaa064581b03809b5d23749309772791e915dc92c06b62fd707c4501eb38","compact":"59694210e1dafeae7fea2a58486c1c079dc5e4fb1459066997bd827198d65b80","nasal":"59694210e1dafeae7fea2a58486c1c079dc5e4fb1459066997bd827198d65b80"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":13,"english":"I have again searched the picture galleries and the sporting-structures, and edifices, and roads passing through gardens, as well as the car.\" Having thought thus, Hanuman again set about searching the subterranean abodes, religious buildings, and many-storied mansions. And flying up, and coming down, and staying, and going at places, and opening doors, and shutting others, and entering and issuing out, and falling down as if darting up, that mighty monkey began to range on all sides.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9ee37d70180715e7a8ad06b685ba44b1c5f8b7ad50fea7815d295414e7c8f80","compact":"e5fea1d92da148fdcb805b4dc3a3a8d5cad5ef2997ff22dd02e9497fc6141eea","nasal":"e5fea1d92da148fdcb805b4dc3a3a8d5cad5ef2997ff22dd02e9497fc6141eea"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":