ings, the holes, and the tanks.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"305bd660934c5bbc2b4980eb872f2c7afdc5471d21d9edc7a978a2b7ebe9ef75","compact":"0701a1feeef6bc370428438a23d5de0d09e6ed05fb6572c646250cfe72fc550a","nasal":"37bbaf77c11160e42d86351c9b3a734bd58cf5e60a9929c956d3d54de6b5cc76"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":19,"english":"And Hanumān saw there Räksasas of various forms, frightful and deformed; but he saw not Janaka's daughter. Hanumān saw there transcendentally beautiful women, daughter of Nāgas, having countenances resembling the moon; but he saw not Janaka's daughter. saw","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-16","DUTT-5-12-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc89d03772c2616f33e8092663363cea3710747c4d8606b5aac947221aa304b7","compact":"c7f8f83a0ef8ced808505fd8de9efa30e2cf532a0bab29eb9cc0aa5ffe481a14","nasal":"c7f8f83a0ef8ced808505fd8de9efa30e2cf532a0bab29eb9cc0aa5ffe481a14"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-10-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":10,"verse":20,"english":"Hanuman there the the foremost and beautiful wives of Vidyadharas; but he saw not Rāghava's beloved Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-12-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5010020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d9fb9532a4f03723949355ec3d4d94a845d93db8a84d4913d79d1324b9470e6","compact":"b82d9d92d9b2630bd6fa1f73bb1972b6afa83e8cc79434c109f631e9f3866137","nasal":"b0d43b59b8b02609c8987c70